description: "Choose meaningful checks and distinguish source checks from runtime verification"
globs: "{apps,packages,scripts}/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,cjs,mjs}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Verification

- Run the package's existing commands from its directory. Read package.json before selecting a script; API lint currently includes --fix, so use a non-mutating lint command for review-only work.
- Prefer the affected test/helper over unrelated suites. Use synthetic data and avoid external side effects. No tests that only mirror source wording.
- Translation changes: run rtk proxy node scripts/check-i18n.cjs from the root and inspect changed callers. Validation must resolve the active locale after module import.
- Instruction changes: run rtk proxy node scripts/check-agent-assets.cjs. This validates structure and references, not behavioral perfection.
- Distinguish source typecheck, generated route validation, build, and browser checks. A malformed .next file is not permission to edit generated code or claim a full pass after excluding it.
- Follow ironbee-devtools-use.mdc for browser work. If the configured tools are unavailable, report that limitation, complete other checks, and do not substitute an unauthorized browser tool.
- Stop only processes you started unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.
